== Boss Fight ==
'''Kuudra's''' boss fight consists of multiple phases, depending on the selected tier.

=== Phase 1: Crates ===
'''Phase One''' involves using a Lava Rod to fish up '''Supply Crates''' in the lava surrounding the main platform and bringing them to the center of the arena. Players can either use a {{Item|Starter Lava Rod}}, {{Item|Topaz Rod}}, {{Item|Magma Rod}}, {{Item|Inferno Rod}}, or {{Item|Hellfire Rod}} to fish up the crates; those lacking a Lava Rod can purchase an '''Elle's Lava Rod''' from the Perk Shop.

Once the supply crate reaches the platform, players must stand still until the meter reaches {{Green|100%}} to pick up the crate. To reduce the time taken to fish and pick up supply crates, one can upgrade the [[File:Chest.png|26px]] '''Steady Hands''' perk unlocked from the [[File:Diamond Sword.png|26px]] '''{{Red|Specialist}}''' route and have a {{Item|Kuudra's Kidney}}, {{Item|Kuudra's Lung}}, or {{Item|Kuudra's Heart}} in their inventory or [[Accessory Bag]].

Taking too long to place the supply crate or taking too much damage will cause the crate to fall back into the lava.

=== Phase 2: Ballista ===
'''Phase Two''' involves building the '''Ballista''' by using the supplies obtained during Phase One. By '''sneaking''' and '''left-clicking''' the piles of supplies on the ground, players make progress towards completing the construction of the Ballista, which occurs once the meter reaches {{Green|100%}}. The Ballista will be the primary weapon that players use against Kuudra.

To reduce the time taken to build the Ballista, one can upgrade the [[File:Crafting Table.png|26px]] '''Ballista Mechanic''' perk unlocked from the [[File:Diamond Sword.png|26px]] '''{{Red|Specialist}}''' route or have a {{Item|Kuudra's Kidney}}, {{Item|Kuudra's Lung}}, or {{Item|Kuudra's Heart}} in their inventory or [[Accessory Bag]].

During this phase, mobs will attempt to attack the Ballista, bringing the meter back down to {{Red|0%}}.

=== Phase 3: Fuel ===
'''Phase Three''' involves fishing up '''Fuel Cells''' to fuel the Ballista constructed during Phase Two. They can be fished up with a Lava Rod, similar to supply crates, and are used with the Ballista to attack Kuudra. Once all {{Green|4}} Fuel Cells have been secured, players can mount the Ballista and fire at Kuudra.

To reduce the time taken to fish up Fuel Cells, one can upgrade the [[File:Chest.png|26px]] '''Steady Hands''' perk unlocked from the [[File:Diamond Sword.png|26px]] '''{{Red|Specialist}}''' route.

During Burning Tier Kuudra and above, Kuudra must be stunned before the Ballista can be fired: otherwise, very little damage will be dealt and Kuudra will submerge.

=== Phase 4: Stomach ===
[[File:Kuudra's Stomach.png|thumb|Kuudra's stomach]]

'''Phase Four''' is exclusive to '''Burning''' Tier and higher, and involves players firing themselves into Kuudra's stomach. In order to enter Kuudra's stomach, players can either:

* Purchase a [[File:Cannoneer.png|26px]] '''Human Cannonball''', allowing you to fire yourself into Kuudra's mouth;
* Stand in the '''Consumption Zone''', allowing yourself to be consumed by Kuudra's tentacles.

Several '''Orbs''' can be found in Kuudra's stomach, which must be broken to stun Kuudra. Breaking the orbs with a Pickaxe will reduce their health by {{Green|5%}}; players who do not have a Pickaxe can purchase a '''Elle's Pickaxe''' in the Kuudra Perk Shop.

During this time, several {{MobSprite|Magma Bacteria}} will spawn, who fire projectiles at the player that deal knockback. When Kuudra submerges, the stomach will fill up with lava and all players within will be launched out.

=== Phase 5: Lair ===
[[File:Kuudra's Hollow Infernal Tier.png|thumb|Kuudra's true lair]]

'''Phase Five''' is exclusive to the '''Infernal''' Tier that begins once Kuudra's health reaches {{Red|25%}}. It involves players dodging Kuudra's tentacles and firing at Kuudra's head until its health reaches {{Red|0}}.

The main arena of {{Zone|Kuudra's Hollow}} collapses to reveal a lower section surrounded by lava, with {{MobSprite|Wandering Blaze}}s surrounding the top of the arena, killing any players above them.

During this phase, all deaths are considered '''Final Kills''': however, players can revive if their party has a member alive who has the [[File:Support Route.png|26px]] '''{{Red|Support}}''' Route selected, who can revive players using {{Tokens}}.

